Hal Work (halw@hpwrce.mayfield.hp.com) wrote:
: I downloaded the binaries last night for the 3.13 Amiga release.  But, when
: I attempted to extract the files, lz 2.0 gave me a 'bad header checksum'
: error on both of the lzh files.  Got 1 file out of the first, but the second
: croaked completely.  Am I using an out-of-date lz.  what's the poop?

	LZ 2.0 was a bogus patch to an earlier LZ. The current version of LZ
is 1.92, and has been for a year or more. A much better choice would be to use
LhA (current version is 1.38 eval or 1.42 registered). LhA will handle more
compression schemes than LZ will.


